---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { newsletter, site } from '../config/site';
---

<Layout title="Privacy" description="What Cueory stores, what it doesn't, and how to delete or export your data.">
  <Prose>
    <h1>Privacy, in plain language</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">Draft for review. Last updated: not yet published.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      We keep only what we need. We don't sell your data, we don't show ads, and we don't use trackers that follow you to
      other websites.
    </p>

    <h2>Right now</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} has no accounts yet. You can read lessons without giving us anything. Nothing you do on a lesson is
      saved.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you pick Light or Dark at the bottom of a page, your browser remembers that choice on your device. It never
      reaches us.
    </p>

    <h2>Launch-updates emails</h2>
    <p>
      If you sign up for launch updates, your email address is stored by {newsletter.provider}, the service that sends
      those emails for us. You'll get a confirmation email first, and every email has an unsubscribe link. We use your
      address only for {site.name} updates.
    </p>

    <h2>Visit statistics</h2>
    <p>
      We count page visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics. It doesn't use cookies, and it doesn't build a profile of you.
    </p>

    <h2>When accounts arrive</h2>
    <p>Accounts are coming later. When they do, this page will be updated first. We plan to store only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your email address, so you can sign in.</li>
      <li>A display name, if you choose one.</li>
      <li>Your answers to a few setup questions, such as your exam date.</li>
      <li>Your study progress: what you've studied, your answers, and when to review next.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your account page will have one button that deletes your account and everything linked to it, and one that
      downloads a copy of your data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who handles data for us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cloudflare hosts the website and counts visits.</li>
      <li>{newsletter.provider} stores newsletter signups and sends launch-update emails.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>. You can ask what we hold about you or ask us
      to delete it.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
